# FinScale: Financial Risk Classification (Single-Node Prototype)

Fine-tunes Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct with LoRA (MLX) to classify financial
disclosures into structured JSON (category, severity, explanation), then
compares base vs fine-tuned on a held-out test set.

This is the single-node baseline for a planned multi-node run on
NVIDIA GB10 systems (PyTorch + NCCL, orchestrated by Fuzzball).

## Requirements
- Apple Silicon Mac (tested: MacBook Pro, M4 Pro, 24 GB RAM)
- macOS, Python 3.11, Conda
- ~10 GB free disk (model + cache)
- Internet access for the first model download

## Setup
```bash
git clone https://github.com/<your-user>/finscale.git
cd finscale
conda create -n finscale python=3.11 -y
conda activate finscale
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

Optional but recommended (avoids slow, rate-limited downloads):
```bash
export HF_TOKEN=<your_huggingface_token>
hf download Qwen/Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct
```

## Run
Run the steps in order from the repo root.

1. Generate labeled data (writes `data/train_raw.jsonl`)
   ```bash
   python make_data.py
   ```
2. Validate, deduplicate, split, and fine-tune (LoRA, 100 iterations)
   ```bash
   python train.py
   ```
3. Evaluate base vs fine-tuned on the held-out test set
   ```bash
   python evaluate.py
   ```

## Expected results (reference run, n=32 test examples)

| Model | Valid JSON | Category acc. | Category macro-F1 | Severity acc. |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Base | 68.8% | 53.1% | 0.519 | 71.9% |
| Fine-tuned | 96.9% | 71.9% | 0.577 | 71.9% |

Exact numbers will vary slightly with data generation and random seeds.

## Pipeline details
- Data: 327 records, 321 unique after dedup, split 256 train / 33 valid / 32 test.
- LoRA: 8 layers, rank 8, Adam, lr 1e-5, batch size 2, 100 iterations, max seq 4096.
- Trainable parameters: 3.3M of 3.09B (0.108%).
- Throughput on M4 Pro: about 420 to 545 tokens/sec.

## Troubleshooting
- **Download looks stuck / "Still waiting to acquire lock":** another process is
  downloading the same model. Stop all of them (`ps aux | grep python`), then
  re-run. Note that `Ctrl+Z` only suspends a process; use `Ctrl+C` to stop it.
- **`evaluate.py` shows no output for several minutes:** it is generating
  silently. Check it is alive with `ps aux | grep evaluate | grep -v grep`.
  Expect roughly 5 to 15 minutes.
- **`EnvironmentNameNotFound: finscale`:** create the env first (see Setup).

## Limitations
- Small test set (32), so results are directional, not statistically robust.
- Labels are model-generated and may contain noise.
- Rare classes (liquidity, supply_chain, credit) are underrepresented.

## Roadmap
- More data for rare categories; larger test set; human label review.
- Longer training, higher LoRA rank, learning-rate sweep.
- Port to PyTorch + PEFT/NeMo with NCCL on dual GB10 nodes; measure scaling
  efficiency; serve via an OpenAI-compatible endpoint with Fuzzball.

## Data and licensing
Public, non-proprietary financial text and synthetic examples only.
Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct is subject to its own license on Hugging Face.
